.* WRKJRN: the journals a name selects, with the recovery options.
:PNLGRP.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=TEXTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 50'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=JRN CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=JRNLIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=ASPDEV CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=JRNTEXT CLASS=TEXTCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=JRNS VARS='OPT JRN JRNLIB ASPDEV JRNTEXT'.
:KEYL HELP='KEYS/WJKEYS' NAME=WJKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKJRN KEYL=WJKEYS HELP=WRKJRN ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SPACE.Work with Journals
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=JRNS.(No journals match specified name)
:LISTACT HELP='WRKJRN/OPTIONS' OPTION=2 ENTER='CMD ?APYJRNCHG JRN(&JRNLIB./&JRN.)'.2=Forward recovery
:LISTACT HELP='WRKJRN/OPTIONS' OPTION=3 ENTER='CMD ?RMVJRNCHG JRN(&JRNLIB./&JRN.)'.3=Backout recovery
:LISTACT HELP='WRKJRN/OPTIONS' OPTION=5 ENTER='CMD WRKJRNA JRN(&JRNLIB./&JRN.)'.5=Display journal status
:LISTACT HELP='WRKJRN/OPTIONS' OPTION=6 ENTER='RETURN 6'.6=Recover damaged journal
:LISTACT HELP='WRKJRN/OPTIONS' OPTION=7 ENTER='RETURN 7'.7=Recover damaged journal receivers
:LISTACT HELP='WRKJRN/OPTIONS' OPTION=8 ENTER='CMD WRKJRNA JRN(&JRNLIB./&JRN.)'.8=Work with journal attributes
:LISTACT HELP='WRKJRN/OPTIONS' OPTION=9 ENTER='RETURN 9'.9=Associate receivers with journal
:LISTCOL HELP='WRKJRN/OPT' VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Opt
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/JRN' VAR=JRN USAGE=OUTPUT.Journal
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/JRNLIB' VAR=JRNLIB USAGE=OUTPUT.Library
:LISTGRP COL=ASPGRP.ASP
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/ASPDEV' VAR=ASPDEV USAGE=OUTPUT.Device
:ELISTGRP.
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/JRNTEXT' VAR=JRNTEXT USAGE=OUTPUT.Text
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKJRN.Work with Journals - Help
:P.The journals the name selects. Option 2 applies journaled changes
to the files, option 3 takes them back out; options 5 and 8 show the
journal's receivers and the objects it covers.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/WJKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKJRN/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JRN'.Journal
:P.The journal, by name and library.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JRNLIB'.Library
:P.The library of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ASPDEV'.ASP device
:P.The ASP device of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JRNTEXT'.Text
:P.The text of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKJRN/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.2=Forward recovery
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to forward recovery it. The
Apply Journaled Changes (APYJRNCHG) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.3=Backout recovery
:PD.Type 3 next to an entry and press Enter to backout recovery it. The
Remove Journaled Changes (RMVJRNCHG) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.5=Display journal status
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display journal status
it. The Work with Journal Attributes (WRKJRNA) command runs for the
entry.
:PT.6=Recover damaged journal
:PD.Type 6 next to an entry and press Enter to recover damaged journal
it.
:PT.7=Recover damaged journal receivers
:PD.Type 7 next to an entry and press Enter to recover damaged journal
receivers it.
:PT.8=Work with journal attributes
:PD.Type 8 next to an entry and press Enter to work with journal
attributes it. The Work with Journal Attributes (WRKJRNA) command runs
for the entry.
:PT.9=Associate receivers with journal
:PD.Type 9 next to an entry and press Enter to associate receivers with
journal it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
